{"is_source_file": true, "format": "Python", "description": "This file defines the GUI component for a mapping tool used within the BORIS behavioral observation software. It includes a window class `ModifiersCodingMapWindow` with an internal view class for rendering and interacting with graphical polygons over a map image. The class allows loading a map, displaying defined polygon areas with specified colors, and selecting/deselecting areas by clicking on them. It handles image loading, polygon rendering, and user interactions for coding behaviors via graphical regions.", "external_files": ["PySide6.QtCore", "PySide6.QtGui", "PySide6.QtWidgets", "binascii"], "external_methods": ["binascii.a2b_base64", "QPixmap.loadFromData"], "published": ["Signals: mousePress"], "classes": [{"name": "ModifiersCodingMapWindow", "description": "Main dialog window for displaying and interacting with the coding map, loading the map image, and managing polygon areas."}, {"name": "ModifiersCodingMapWindow.View", "description": "A custom QGraphicsView subclass that emits a signal upon mouse press events to enable interaction with the polygon areas."}], "methods": [{"name": "loadMap(self)", "description": "Loads a base64-encoded bitmap from the coding map data, displays it, and overlays polygons representing different coded areas.", "scope": "ModifiersCodingMapWindow", "scopeKind": "class"}, {"name": "viewMousePressEvent(self, event)", "description": "Handles mouse press events within the view, toggling the selection status of polygon areas based on user clicks.", "scope": "ModifiersCodingMapWindow", "scopeKind": "class"}, {"name": "getCodes(self)", "description": "Returns the current comma-separated list of selected area codes.", "scope": "ModifiersCodingMapWindow", "scopeKind": "class"}, {"name": "__init__(self, parent)", "scope": "ModifiersCodingMapWindow.View", "scopeKind": "class", "description": "unavailable"}, {"name": "__init__(self, modifiers_coding_map)", "scope": "ModifiersCodin